---
import Legal from '../../layouts/Legal.astro';
const EMAIL = 'tyler@btso.dev';
---
<Legal
  pageTitle="Privacy Policy | PlateIFR: IFR Plates & Holds"
  heading="PlateIFR privacy"
  description="What PlateIFR keeps on your device, what it sends, and what it never does."
  lastUpdated="November 24, 2026"
>
  <p>
    PlateIFR is an offline-first FAA Instrument Rating (IRA) study app and cockpit procedures
    trainer for iPhone, Android and the web. It has no user accounts, no ads, no third-party
    analytics and no cross-app tracking. PlateIFR uses public-domain FAA materials from faa.gov for
    training only (not for navigation) and is not affiliated with or endorsed by the Federal
    Aviation Administration.
  </p>

  <h2>Your study progress stays on your device</h2>
  <p>
    Your answered questions, spaced-repetition intervals, completed approach plate lessons, holding
    and VOR drill counts, mock exam history, exam date target and theme preference are stored
    locally on your device (SQLite on iOS and Android, localStorage on the web). We do not operate a
    backend server and do not upload your study data anywhere. If your device backs up app data to
    iCloud or Google Backup, Apple or Google handles those backups under your account.
  </p>

  <h2>One-time Pro purchase</h2>
  <p>
    PlateIFR offers a single optional one-time in-app purchase to unlock all 12 FAA approach plates
    and enroute charts, 420 source-cited IRA questions and unlimited 60-question mock exams. Payment
    is handled by the Apple App Store or Google Play; we never see your card or payment details. To
    verify and restore your purchase across reinstalls, the app uses
    <a href="https://www.revenuecat.com/privacy">RevenueCat</a>, which receives a random anonymous
    app user ID generated on your device, your purchase receipt and basic technical details such as
    app version, device type and store storefront. This information is used solely to unlock and
    restore your purchase.
  </p>

  <h2>Optional live airport weather lookup</h2>
  <p>
    Inside the METAR decoder on iOS and Android, you can optionally type a 4-letter airport ICAO
    code (such as KPDX) and tap Fetch Live to request the current public METAR directly from the
    National Weather Service Aviation Weather Center (<a href="https://aviationweather.gov">aviationweather.gov</a>).
    No personal data or location is sent; only the 4-letter station code you entered is requested.
    All bundled IFR METAR samples, the 1-2-3 alternate calculator, holding simulator, VOR/HSI lab
    and every plate lesson work offline without making any network requests.
  </p>

  <h2>What we don't do</h2>
  <p>
    We do not sell or share your information, show advertisements, embed ad SDKs or third-party
    analytics, track you across apps or websites, or collect your name, email address, contacts,
    location, photos or microphone.
  </p>

  <h2>Children</h2>
  <p>
    PlateIFR is intended for prospective and certificated instrument pilots and does not knowingly
    collect personal information from children under 13.
  </p>

  <h2>Deleting your data</h2>
  <p>
    You can clear all local study progress anytime from Readiness &rarr; Reset Study Progress, or by
    uninstalling the app. To request deletion of anonymous purchase records held by RevenueCat, email
    <a href={`mailto:${EMAIL}`}>{EMAIL}</a>. Your Apple or Google store account retains its own
    purchase history.
  </p>

  <h2>Changes and contact</h2>
  <p>
    If this policy changes, the date at the top of this page will be updated. Questions or support
    requests can be sent to <a href={`mailto:${EMAIL}`}>{EMAIL}</a>.
  </p>
</Legal>
